  style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>NON REACTIVE<b>\/\r\n  REACTIVE<\/b><\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=196 valign=top style='width:146.65pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\r\n  height:13.5pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US style='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>NON\r\n  REACTIVE<\/span><span lang=EN-US>\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 (&lt; 9)<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n <\/tr>\r\n <tr style='height:12.75pt'>\r\n  <td width=223 valign=top style='width:167.1pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\r\n  height:12.75pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:9.0pt'>(enzyme \u2013linked\r\n  immunosorbent assay )<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=94 valign=top style='width:70.4pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\r\n  height:12.75pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><span lang=EN-US\r\n  style='font-size:9.0pt'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=236 valign=top style='width:177.2pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\r\n  height:12.75pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><span lang=EN-US\r\n  style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=196 valign=top style='width:146.65pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\r\n  height:12.75pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US>EQUIVOCAL (9 - 11)<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n <\/tr>\r\n <tr style='height:12.75pt'>\r\n  <td width=223 valign=top style='width:167.1pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\r\n  height:12.75pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\r\n  \"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=94 valign=top style='width:70.4pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\r\n  height:12.75pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><span lang=EN-US\r\n  style='font-size:8.0pt'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=236 valign=top style='width:177.2pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\r\n  height:12.75pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><span lang=EN-US\r\n  style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=196 valign=top style='width:146.65pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\r\n  height:12.75pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US>REACTIVE\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 (&gt; 11)<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n <\/tr>\r\n <tr style='height:12.75pt'>\r\n  <td width=223 valign=top style='width:167.1pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\r\n  height:12.75pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:8.0pt'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=94 valign=top style='width:70.4pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\r\n  height:12.75pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><b><span\r\n  lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=236 valign=top style='width:177.2pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\r\n  height:12.75pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><span lang=EN-US\r\n  style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=196 valign=top style='width:146.65pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\r\n  height:12.75pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n <\/tr>\r\n<\/table>\r\n\r\n<\/div>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><u><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'><span style='text-decoration:\r\n none'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/span><\/u><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><u><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>Introduction:<\/span><\/u><\/b><span\r\nlang=EN-US style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'> <\/span><span\r\nlang=EN-US style='font-size:8.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>Dengue\r\nvirus is a flavivirus found largely in areas of the tropic and sub-tropics.\r\nThere are four distinct but antigenically related serotypes of dengue viruses,\r\nand transmission is by mosquito, principally Aedes aegypti and Aedes\r\nalbopictus.<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:8.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>The\r\nmosquito-borne dengue viruses (serotype 1-4) cause dengue fever, a severe\r\nflu-like illness. The disease is prevalent in third world tropical regions and\r\nspreading to sub-tropical developed countries - including the United States.\r\nWHO estimates that 50-80 million cases of dengue fever occur worldwide each\r\nyear, including a potentially deadly form of the disease called Dengue\r\nHemorrhagic Fever (<b>DFH<\/b>) and Dengue Shock Syndrome (<b>DSS<\/b>). Primary\r\ninfection with dengue virus results in a self-limiting disease characterized by\r\nmild to high fever lasting 3 to 7 days, severe headache with pain behind the\r\neyes, muscle and joint pain, rash and vomiting. Secondary infection is the more\r\ncommon form of the disease in many parts of Southeast Asia and South America.\r\nIgM antibodies are not detectable until 5-10 days in case of primary dengue\r\ninfection and until 4-5 days in secondary infection after the onset of illness.\r\nIgG appear after 14 days and persist for life in case of primary infection and\r\nrise within 1-2 days after the onset of symptoms in secondary infection. This\r\nform of the disease is more serious and in DHF and DSS. The major clinical\r\nsymptoms can include high fever, hemorrhagic events, and circulatory failure,\r\nand the fatality rate can be as high as 40 %. Early diagnosis of DSS is\r\nparticularly important, as patients may die within 12 to 24 hours if\r\nappropriate treatment is not administered.<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:8.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>Primary dengue\r\nvirus infection is characterized by elevations in specific IgM antibody levels\r\n3 to 5 days after the onset of symptoms; this generally persists upto 30 to 60\r\ndays. IgG levels also become elevated after 10 to 14 days and remain detectable\r\nfor life. During secondary infection, IgM levels generally rise more slowly and\r\nreach lower levels than in primary infection, while IgG levels rise rapidly\r\nfrom 1 to 2 days after onset symptoms.<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US style='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>DRAWN\r\nSAMPLE FROM OUTSIDE<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\r\n\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>Lisa Scan-EM (Semi-Automated Clinical ELISA\r\nAnalyzer)<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<\/div>","page":{"size":"612.0pt 792.0pt","margin":"153.0pt 36.0pt 72.0pt 36.0pt"}}